# Frontend (Next.js)

## App Router pages

| Route | File |
|-------|------|
| `/` | `app/page.tsx` |
| `/login`, `/register` | `app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, `register/page.tsx` |
| `/dashboard` | `app/dashboard/page.tsx` |
| `/dashboard/inbox` | `app/dashboard/inbox/page.tsx` |
| `/dashboard/vault` | `app/dashboard/vault/page.tsx` |
| `/dashboard/add` | `app/dashboard/add/page.tsx` |
| `/dashboard/settings` | `app/dashboard/settings/page.tsx` |

Shell: `app/dashboard/layout.tsx` (nav).

## API & auth

- **Single client**: `lib/api.ts` — export `api` object; never duplicate fetch logic in pages
- **Types**: `lib/types.ts` — keep in sync with backend DTOs
- Base URL: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` (default `/api`)
- JWT: `localStorage.getItem('token')` + cookie fallback in `fetchWithAuth`
- Server rewrite: `next.config.ts` → `INTERNAL_API_URL` (Docker: `http://backend:8080`)

## Components

- Inbox: `InboxCard.tsx`, `InboxDetailModal.tsx`
- Vault: `VaultCard.tsx`, `VaultDetailModal.tsx`
- Theme: `lib/ThemeProvider.tsx`, `lib/categoryColor.ts`

## Patterns

- Client components for interactive dashboard views; use `api.*` helpers
- Pagination query params: `PageNumber`, `PageSize`, `SearchTerm`, optional `CategoryId`
- Resource status PATCH body: `{ status: number }` — enum matches backend `ResourceStatus`

## Adding UI

1. Add method to `lib/api.ts`
2. Add/update interface in `lib/types.ts`
3. Page under `app/dashboard/` or shared component in `components/`

Run dev (outside Docker): `npm run dev` in `knowledgeos-frontend/`.
